{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299","id":4888152132,"node_id":"PR_kwDOROLhSM8AAAABI1tIRA","html_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299","diff_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/issues/299","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/issues/299/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/statuses/153f10e6bac02b1a962213431141fd1c54906e99","number":299,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(labels): QR, Code128 and audited reprints (#208)","user":{"login":"yigini","id":32960535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYwNTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32960535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini","html_url":"https://github.com/yigini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"References #208.\n\nSample, container and aliquot labels use the exact issued identity in both QR and Code128. One scoped server command commits an immutable `LabelPrintEvent` before the browser print dialog opens; reprints require a reason. Print-time permission/state checks and SQL guards protect identity, counts, ordering, scope and historical evidence, with localized errors in all five locales.\n\nThe supported predecessor can lack the four approved #180 schema objects. A guarded schema owner now installs the unchanged approved DDL before #206 containers and #208 labels only when all four objects are absent. Canonical or exact Prisma storage is a no-op; partial/modified storage refuses. It adds no sequence rows, backfill, code allocation, renumbering or receipt writes. The scanner adds only the digest-bound owner entry, with no writer exemption.\n\nThe readiness preservation comparator permits only the exact appended nullable TEXT/no-default `Sample.labSampleCode`, NULL for existing rows. Every old column/value, row and receipt remains protected. Other schema additions, changed types/defaults/constraints, old-value changes and non-NULL backfills refuse; the unchanged old SQL is compared verbatim after removing only that one canonical column declaration.\n\nLabel sizes are preserved, with larger stock required when Code128 modules would fall below0.19mm. Documentation records the ISO7064 MOD37,36 hybrid system's adjacent-transposition limitation. Physical printer/scanner acceptance remains pending. A retained print event can reach the existing generic500 deletion response when a RESTRICT foreign key prevents preanalytic deletion; deletion authority is unchanged.\n\nValidation of exact head `153f10e6bac02b1a962213431141fd1c54906e99` / tree `34f6d9be9c00b2fd923989e4d4291a06ec333e32` / base `be8379745bdfae52ce46496ff26514dc7d729640`:\n\n- [Ordinary CI38953786365, attempt1](https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/actions/runs/38953786365): **376 suites /5,761 tests passed**,1838.22s. Client/theme, BOTH real candidate/supported-baseline Docker builds, all five boundary scenarios and full real deployment-readiness acceptance passed.\n- Frozen ordinary LOCAL full:376 suites /5,761 tests passed,13327.782s. The final comparator correction passed4 focused suites /190 tests. Client build and lint passed with0errors/14existing warnings.\n- Parent independently verified every test reporter line between original ZIP and full CI log, exact376-suite frozen discovery, all22archive entries and20closed evidence files. [Closed originals and independent review](https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/blob/59cd49393e5fce07b5a2bfe0c51610e26702c07a/WP/backlog-resume-20261013/issue208-ci38953786365-parent-once/publication-index.json).\n\nWindows LOCAL tests used a retained visible Temp fixture with both ordinary setup files, stock assertions and repository CI/Jest rules unchanged. Frozen mapped inputs/runtime files and the read-only scanner index were checked before/after. The sole generated help manifest was retained and restored only after full closure. The final two-file correction matches tested working bytes exactly for the contract and solely CRLF-to-LF for the readiness script. Approved #180 owner/loader/DDL pins are unchanged.\n\nOriginal CI38898578537 and38915551182 remain immutable FAILED runs, never retried. The latter's original row/receipt payloads were not emitted, so their sole mismatch and equality remain unknown; this new exact-tree real readiness result does not retrospectively change either failure.\n\n[Exact-head source audit passed](https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299#issuecomment-6224793665) at `153f10e6bac02b1a962213431141fd1c54906e99`. Actual post-deploy acceptance remains pending. All main merges remain held until the actual be837974 release deployment and Claudio postcheck PASS. This PR has no automatic closing references; #208 stays open for actual acceptance.\n\n\n### Deferred following the exact-head source audit\n\n- Queue a small forward follow-up after the current release: `removePreAnalyticSample` must return a stable409 retained-evidence code when print events or containers exist. The current RESTRICT protection rolls the transaction back and can return generic500; no evidence is deleted. This follow-up is deferred and no additional code change is included here.\n- Batch preview can fail the whole batch with409 `LABEL_PRINT_CODE_REQUIRED` without identifying the uncoded row. Naming that row or preselecting coded rows is deferred.\n- Samples without issued codes no longer have pre-arrival labels. This visible reception change must be shown to YY before a future #208 deployment gate.\n- Print buttons in `SamplesTable.jsx` and `SampleSummary.jsx` do not yet hide or disable based on `PRINT_LABELS`. The server enforces the permission and returns a localized refusal; UI polish is deferred.\n- A future #208 release kit must retain authorized-production-copy DRY results and classifications for both `install_sample_code_schema` and `install_label_print_events`, and budget every extra read-only temporary DB snapshot on each default startup. Physical printer/scanner acceptance remains pending. The current be837974 release kit remains #206/#214/#209 only.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T12:09:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T21:19:44Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ca0de122750de6bdc9ef8f878818959f6631330a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"yigini:codex/issue-208-labels","ref":"codex/issue-208-labels","repo":{"id":1155719496,"node_id":"R_kgDOROLhSA","name":"soilfer-lims","full_name":"yigini/soilfer-lims","owner":{"login":"yigini","id":32960535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYwNTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32960535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini","html_url":"https://github.com/yigini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yi